  "query_preview": "..\nSouthwest of the region, a tropical disturbance, Invest 99W, is \nwithin a developing monsoon pattern in Yap State. The Marianas\nremain in the northern periphery of this unsettled pattern with\nonly scattered showers moving across Guam this afternoon. Depending \non the development and a gradual northwestward track of 99W, showers \nare expected to build across the converging monsoon and trade-wind \npatterns in its wake, bringing scattered to numerous locally heavy \nshowers and isolated thunderstorms to the Marianas by midweek. \nConvectively-driven gusts to 25 mph are expected with heavier \nshowers, with hi-res model guidance suggesting occasional gusts to 30\nmph. Although there still remains some uncertainty in this outcome, \nwhere the actual speed, strength, and track of 99W will determine how\nclose in proximity the trailing convergence is to the Marianas.",
